882:\section{Conclusions}\label{s-con}
884:Our complexity study led to three complete and three almost complete complexity classifications (Theorems~\ref{t-acyclic}--\ref{t-injective}). Due to our systematic approach we were able to identify a number of open questions for future research, which we collect below.
886:In Lemma~\ref{l-girth} we prove that for every $k\geq 3$ and every $g\geq 3$, \textsc{Acyclic $k$-Colouring} is \NP-complete for graphs of girth at least~$g$.
888:We recall that \textsc{Injective $3$-Colouring} is polynomial-time solvable for general graphs.
889:Moreover, for every $k\geq 4$, \textsc{Injective $k$-Colouring} is \NP-complete for bipartite graphs (by Lemma~\ref{l-triangle}) and thus for graphs of girth at least~$4$.
898:We have made progress for the corresponding high-girth problem for \textsc{Star $3$-Colouring} in Lemma~\ref{lem:star-col-high-girth}.
901:\textsc{Star $k$-Colouring} is \NP-complete for bipartite graphs~\cite{ACKKR04} and thus for graphs of girth at least~$4$.
910:We note that the graph $G'$ in the proof of Lemma~\ref{l-5p1} contains an induced $2P_1+P_4$.
921:Recall that \textsc{Injective Colouring} and \textsc{Colouring} are \NP-complete for $2P_2$-free graphs.
925:The class of split graphs coincides with the class of $(2P_2,C_4,C_5)$-free graphs~\cite{FH77} and thus \textsc{Acyclic Colouring} is equivalent to \textsc{Colouring} for split graphs, and hence it is polynomial-time solvable.
940:The general distance constrained labelling problem \textsc{$L(a_1,\ldots,a_p)$-Labelling} is to decide if a graph $G$ has a labelling $c:V(G)\to \{1,\ldots,k\}$ for some integer $k\geq 1$ such that for every $i\in \{1,\ldots,p\}$, $|c(u)-c(v)|\geq a_i$ whenever $u$ and $v$ are two vertices of distance~$i$ in $G$ (in this setting, it is usually assumed that $a_1\geq \ldots \geq a_p$). If $k$ is fixed, we write \textsc{$L(a_1,\ldots,a_p)$-$k$-Labelling} instead. By applying Theorem~\ref{t-general} we obtain the following result.
943:For all $k\geq 1, a_1\geq 1,\ldots, a_k\geq 1$, the {\sc $L(a_1,\ldots,a_p)$-$k$-Labelling} problem is polynomial-time solvable for $H$-free graphs if $H$ is a linear forest.
